WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:16.940 --> 00:00:19.800
There are two special cases we need to look at

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:24.400
while finding the 'HCF' and 'LCM' of two numbers.

00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:28.780
First case, when one number is a multiple of the other.

00:00:28.940 --> 00:00:33.700
And second, when they have no common factors except one.

00:00:33.940 --> 00:00:36.480
Which means they are co-prime.

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:39.400
Let's understand the cases in detail.

00:00:39.820 --> 00:00:42.420
The first case would have numbers like

00:00:42.420 --> 00:00:46.420
four and eight, eight is a multiple of four.

00:00:46.760 --> 00:00:52.740
Or numbers like 21 and 7, 21 is a multiple of seven.

00:00:53.060 --> 00:00:56.400
One number is a multiple of the other.

00:00:56.640 --> 00:01:00.520
Why is it a special case? It's because in such cases

00:01:00.720 --> 00:01:03.660
the 'LCM' is always the greater number.

00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:08.040
The 'LCM' of four and eight will be eight.

00:01:08.140 --> 00:01:13.660
And the 'LCM' of 21 and 7, will be 21.

00:01:13.980 --> 00:01:17.800
And the 'HCF' will always be the smaller number.

00:01:17.800 --> 00:01:21.700
The 'HCF' of these two numbers will be 4.

00:01:21.780 --> 00:01:26.980
And the 'HCF' of these two numbers will be 7.

00:01:27.260 --> 00:01:29.140
What about the second case ?

00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:34.540
An example of two co-prime numbers, would be 4 and 7.

00:01:34.780 --> 00:01:37.140
Or 3 &amp; 5.

00:01:37.140 --> 00:01:42.480
Both these pairs have no common factors except one.

00:01:42.740 --> 00:01:47.340
What is so special about 'LCM' and 'HCF' of such numbers?

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:50.360
Well the 'LCM' of such numbers,

00:01:50.360 --> 00:01:54.180
will always equal the product of the two numbers.

00:01:54.380 --> 00:02:00.800
For the first pair, the 'LCM' will be 4 times 7 which equals 28.

00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:08.220
And for the second pair, the 'LCM' will equal 3 times 5, which equals 15.

00:02:08.460 --> 00:02:11.500
And what will be the 'HCF' of such numbers?

00:02:11.640 --> 00:02:14.860
It will always be 1.

00:02:15.080 --> 00:02:23.500
The HCF of 4 and 7, as well as the HCF of 3 and 5, equals 1.

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:25.020
But remember,

00:02:25.120 --> 00:02:30.780
these techniques should be used only to verify your answers.

